      "type": "text",
      "text": "Unresponsive constipation: disimpact the bowel (oral or rectal agents), then keep a regular diet and stool routine. Infants USU don't need extreme measures; if intervention is required, a glycerin suppository is typically adequate."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
